      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:d4d2b22f26414abb",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: what did kūḍā mean?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: మాత్రమే",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "మాత్రమే (mātramē) — \"only\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "మాత్రమే (mātramē) is the other half of కూడా (kūḍā). Where కూడా (kūḍā) opens an answer out, మాత్రమే (mātramē) shuts it: పెరుగు మాత్రమే (mātramē) is \"curd and nothing else\". It stands in the same place, straight after the thing it is about."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It is built on Sanskrit mātra, \"a measure\" — the same piece English carries in metre and in diameter. Saying మాత్రమే (mātramē) is saying \"this much and no further\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "With a small quantity in front it does polite work. కొంచెం మాత్రమే (mātramē), \"only a little\", accepts what is offered without taking much of it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two, and they pull opposite ways."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "mātramē",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *mātramē*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "it once more, slowly",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: it once more, slowly]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "perugu kūḍā, then perugu mātramē, and say which one takes more",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *perugu kūḍā*, then *perugu mātramē*, and say which one takes more]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
